  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Most Batswana carry a Setswana name with a meaning, often a whole sentence or a thanks: Kagiso (peace), Lesedi (light), Onalenna (He is with us), Kealeboga (I am grateful), Oratile (He loves us). Many of these names are given to boys and girls alike. Alongside it people often have an English or Christian first name (Grace, Godfrey), and either may be the one they go by. Surnames come from the father's line and are mostly Setswana words or the name of a forebear (Molefe, Modise, Kgosidintsi). People are greeted with Rra (sir) and Mma (madam), and a mother is often called Mma plus her first child's name. Ikalanga is the other big home language, mostly in the north east around Francistown; its names are not yet listed here.",
